        <h2>Profile of the University President</h2>
        <p>Dr. Silverio Ramon Dela Cruz Salunson is an esteemed academic leader who currently serves as the President of Tarlac Agricultural University (TAU). Having worked in higher education for more than twenty years, Dr. Salunson has shown outstanding skills in business administration, management information systems, and educational leadership.</p>
        <p>Fondly called Sir Vermon, the second president of TAU was born in Victoria, Tarlac, on 5 November 1977. Since childhood, he was very promising in all his academic pursuits. He had formal schooling from 1984 to 1990 at the Victoria East Central School, and then enrolled at Victoria High School, where he completed his secondary education and laid a strong foundation for his future.</p>
        <p>Beyond his administrative duties, Dr. Salunson wears many hats. He is an educator, inspiring the next generation of business leaders. As a mentor, he directs students and colleagues towards achieving excellence. As an accreditor, he ensures that TAU upholds the highest standards of educational quality. As an innovator, he always seeks new methods of enriching the college experience. As a business incubator, he promotes industry cooperation and entrepreneurship to support students and society at large.</p>
      </div>
