  <!-- TAU UNDER DR. SALUNSON -->
  <section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-wrap oop-prose">
      <h2>TAU under Dr. Salunson: Pioneering the SMART Revolution in Central Luzon</h2>
      <p>Under the new leadership of this visionary president, TAU is at the "threshold of positioning" itself as the frontline model of sustainability and innovation in academia. TAU commits itself to a successful educational setting through infrastructure development, accreditation, relevant research, and modern technology in line with the needs of students, the community, and the industry. This approach prepares graduates for the challenges ahead while positioning TAU as a leader in agricultural education and sustainability, locally and worldwide.</p>
      <p>Dr. Salunson's administration promises to transform TAU into an exemplary institution: a technologically equipped campus with modern amenities, and a hub for research, innovation, and community engagement.</p>

      <h3>A sustainable, green campus</h3>
      <p>The President aims to establish an even greener campus through renewable energy and by developing agro-technopreneurship and labs as innovations in business. In this way, sustainable practices become part of the daily life of each student and stakeholder, helping them understand the value of preserving the environment. Community gardens, solar farm projects, and training programs in modern farming technologies that are both financially feasible and environmentally friendly shall be put in place.</p>

      <h3>Modern infrastructure</h3>
      <p>Improved facilities are crucial to modern academia. Modern technologies will be incorporated into the blueprint of the campus, giving TAU useful sensors, data processing, and reliable internet connection. These ideas will improve how students engage and interact, making instruction more effective in a technology-driven setting while readying students for the global job market.</p>

      <h3>Accreditation and global standards</h3>
      <p>Dr. Salunson focuses on program accreditation, especially AUN-QA and PQA, and continuous ISO recertification to meet global education standards. TAU aims to be globally recognized and respected by ensuring that all its programs meet international standards for quality management systems. This commitment will enhance TAU's reputation and give students a broader selection of courses.</p>

      <h3>Research that serves the community</h3>
      <p>Research goals must be in sync with what the community requires. Part of the President's plan is to create effective SMART research and extension programs suited to both educational purposes and the industries TAU serves. These efforts focus on turning technologies into usable applications, so TAU becomes a tangible tool for local farmers and businesses and supports economic growth in the region.</p>

      <h3>Collaboration</h3>
      <p>Working alongside tech companies, government leaders, and academic institutions, Dr. Salunson aims to give the university a valuable source of educational materials. He is looking for new modes of learning and external funding so that students are prepared for career opportunities in technology-based industries.</p>

      <h3>Training for administrators and staff</h3>
      <p>TAU's current administration is committed to comprehensive training programs for administrators, middle management, and rank-and-file employees. Stakeholders who are knowledgeable in best practices in higher education administration help ensure a supportive and responsive learning environment that enhances students' academic experience.</p>

      <h3>A one-stop center</h3>
      <p>Creating a one-stop center that connects students, faculty, staff, and alumni seamlessly is also a priority. It is expected to simplify registration, course scheduling, academic advising, financial aid, and other vital support services, making TAU a more holistic and integrated university for all stakeholders.</p>

      <h3>IoT across the campus</h3>
      <p>The spread of IoT devices throughout the campus would ensure efficiency and connectivity, with benefits for transportation management, campus navigation, and environmental monitoring. Better use of resources, such as reducing waste through sensors, and smart agricultural practices would improve campus operations and give students an environment in which to explore smart agriculture.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SMART PILLARS -->
  <section class="oop-section" style="border-bottom:0">
    <div class="oop-wrap">
      <h2>Dr. Salunson's visionary journey: making TAU a premier SMART university</h2>
      <p class="oop-lead">In an ever-evolving educational landscape, Dr. Salunson takes a visionary approach to reshaping the role of academic institutions in advancing innovation, sustainability, and community involvement. Under his leadership, TAU strives to fulfill its mission through six attributes that form a SMART university. Every element is crucial in shaping the university's destiny and enhancing its influence on society.</p>
      <ul class="oop-pillars">
        <li><h3>SMART People</h3><div>
          <p>The President emphasizes that every member should contribute to the goals of the university. TAU gives prospective students from all walks of life the opportunity to receive a top-notch education through its dynamic scholarship program.</p>
          <p>Input from various sectors is crucial to this approach. It improves services and promotes a sense of belonging. The university plans to strengthen collaboration and boost its research and community projects through partnerships with diverse partners and nearby companies.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li><h3>SMART Learning</h3><div>
          <p>Thorough training keeps teachers and staff up to date, while extracurricular and academic activities enrich the overall educational experience. Programs will be consistently evaluated so that faculty remain at the forefront of educational quality.</p>
          <p>Fulfilling the university's vision requires a dedicated emphasis on creative teaching methods. The President is committed to accrediting TAU programs to meet strict international educational standards. Advanced Learning Management Systems (LMS) simplify the transition to digital education by supporting modern online learning platforms that cater to different learning styles.</p>
          <p>To show a commitment to accessible education, Dr. Salunson is investing in fiber-optic infrastructure to ensure extensive Wi-Fi coverage across the campus. This enhances students' educational experience and prepares them for the digital landscape they will enter after graduation.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li><h3>SMART Research and Training</h3><div>
          <p>TAU is ready for significant advances in research thanks to the development of SMART research and training programs. The President looks forward to high-quality, quantitative research output while pursuing collaborative SMART research and development programs that build stronger links between academia and industry and deepen engagement with farmers and the agricultural sector.</p>
          <p>To protect the innovations and findings from SMART research, the President is committed to operationalizing the Intellectual Property Rights Office. The SMART Research and Development Agenda will be updated regularly so that research remains relevant and impactful. A vibrant research culture will be developed further by having senior faculty mentor junior researchers, with continuous evaluation of research programs.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li><h3>SMART Environment</h3><div>
          <p>Emphasizing sustainable development, Dr. Salunson is committed to making TAU the first mover in SMART environmental practices. This includes large-scale construction of smart physical infrastructure and upgrading existing buildings to support SMART technologies.</p>
          <p>Advanced waste management systems are an important endeavor and a hallmark of the university's contribution to environmental sustainability. Renewable energy solutions and investment in different energy storage technologies further strengthen the green initiative. Recycling and waste reduction efforts are core to this focus and put TAU at the forefront of sustainable practices.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li><h3>SMART Technology</h3><div>
          <p>To function in a data-centric world, Dr. Salunson identified the need for a place where advanced technology can be integrated into the university's own processes. He has partnered with third parties to establish advanced data centers for better data management and stronger research capabilities.</p>
          <p>Resources are being shifted toward technological advancement, leading to mobile applications and AI tools that enhance learning and operational efficiency. Smart sensors through IoT show TAU's commitment to using technology in pursuit of sustainability, building an intelligent ecosystem within the campus.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li><h3>SMART Security</h3><div>
          <p>Alongside these technologies, the administration of Dr. Salunson is devoted to a secure campus through multidimensional SMART security. Campus-wide Wi-Fi systems and covered pathways will make it safer to move through the grounds.</p>
          <p>Building automation and smart security technologies, including advanced real-time tracking systems, safeguard both students and staff. Rigorous cyber security measures protect data integrity and security for all constituents of the university.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="oop-lead" style="margin-top:32px">With Dr. Salunson at the helm, TAU is becoming a leading SMART university that not only teaches but also makes a significant impact on the community and the world. Through developing intelligent individuals, promoting intelligent education, advancing intelligent research and training, committing to an intelligent environment, incorporating intelligent technology, and guaranteeing intelligent security, TAU is getting ready for a future of innovation, collaboration, and sustainability, setting the stage for a brighter future.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

